WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240 align:start position:19%
And that raises the most thrilling
question of all. Could anything live

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.480 align:start position:19%
there?
On Earth, we assumed all life needed

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.320 align:start position:19%
sunlight until we explored the deep
ocean.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:18.680 align:start position:19%
Miles underwater in total darkness,
entire ecosystems thrive around volcanic

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:23.000 align:start position:19%
vents powered not by the sun but by
chemistry.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:28.080 align:start position:19%
Tube worms, blind shrimp, and microbes
live where no light has ever reached.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:32.080 align:start position:19%
If life can do that on Earth, why not in
the hidden ocean of a rogue planet?

